From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:45:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820: Add CPU DVFS through ACPM

Give each CPU its cluster clock from the ACPM firmware and an OPP table,
so cpufreq-dt can scale the three clusters, and let the thermal zones of
the clusters throttle them.

The levels are the ones the DVFS firmware keeps in its SRAM, within the
limits the vendor gives its cpufreq domains: 442 to 1950 MHz for the
little cluster, 507 to 2210 MHz for the middle one and 520 to 2080 MHz
for the big one.  The vendor allows 2314 and 2400 MHz on the middle
cluster and anything from 2236 MHz on the big one only with the memory
clock raised, and nothing in the kernel moves that clock, so those levels
are left out.  The firmware sets the voltage of each level; the voltages
in the tables are the ones it reports for this unit and only feed the
energy model.

Until now the clusters ran at whatever the bootloader left, 1053, 1222
and 1378 MHz.  Raised by hand to the top of these tables with nothing to
throttle them, the big cluster went from 45 to 99 C in about a minute
under load and the critical trip powered the phone off.  Each cluster
zone therefore gets a passive trip at 85 C, just above the 83 C at which
the vendor starts throttling the big and middle clusters, polled every
100 ms once it is crossed.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820.dtsi | 368 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 364 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

