-	 * Nothing can be throttled yet: without cpufreq or cpuidle there is no
-	 * cooling device.  What is left is a critical trip 15 C below the
-	 * hardware trip of the TMU, so the kernel powers the phone off in order
-	 * before the TMU removes the power.
+	 * The levels the DVFS firmware on the APM keeps for each cluster, within
+	 * the limits the vendor gives its cpufreq domains.  The firmware sets the
+	 * voltage of a level itself; the voltages here are the ones it reports
+	 * for this unit and only feed the energy model.  The levels the vendor
+	 * allows only with the memory clock raised are left out, because nothing
+	 * in the kernel moves that clock.  A request is acknowledged within 1 ms.
+	 */
